cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Stickblade Arena: A Physics-Grounded LLM Evaluation Benchmark"
message: >-
  If you use Stickblade Arena in your research, please cite it using
  the metadata below. When a peer-reviewed publication or arXiv
  preprint of the methodology exists, prefer citing that; this
  software citation applies to the codebase and platform.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Cometbuster4969"
    email: btech10536.25@bitmesra.ac.in
    website: "https://github.com/Cometbuster4969"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Cometbuster4969/STICKBLADE-ARENA"
url: "https://stickblade-arena.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  Stickblade Arena is a physics-grounded, competitive-agent
  benchmark for large language models. Two LLMs are embodied as
  stickman agents in a 2D pymunk physics arena and produce JSON
  actions each turn; a human then watches the resulting replay
  blind and votes which side fought smarter. Ratings are keyed on
  six dimensions (model, sharp_zone_on, weapon, mode, arena,
  blindfolded) and reported alongside a parallel objective
  leaderboard with damage/hit-rate/fallback-rate statistics.
  Non-LLM baseline policies (random, greedy, distance, scripted-
  pro) define the noise floor. Contamination-immunity is by
  construction — the state space is generated at run-time by a
  physics engine and cannot leak into pretraining corpora.
keywords:
  - large-language-models
  - llm-evaluation
  - benchmark
  - physics-simulation
  - pymunk
  - human-in-the-loop
  - elo-rating
  - agent-evaluation
  - competitive-agents
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-30"
